{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0511", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-universally-closed}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a4415b960d15265a38ac428d62a3ff5ae66e5bc1054ab3e7d84a88a3be1a9fe0", "source_text": "Universally closed morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7241a12c86e260f8ca5400825822648a87b34f6a35e25aca947a9ff2aa5a9385", "unit_id": "tag:0511:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0511", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfaee67d46ddd4d888702445be4244f6d5bf5b01389aeba0ea95707e8ecf77c4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1c669b66720370999efdea15bdbc73c1e74cdf23a4b8aa5405dd3c962535db6b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks which is representable by\nalgebraic spaces. In\nProperties of Stacks, Section\n<REF_0001>\nwe have defined what it means for <MATH_0002> to be universally closed.\nHere is another characterization.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:64bf88a023756be510b7eddc702b554e76f7691c23b4bcb8b2fc0982572acd06", "unit_id": "tag:0511:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0511", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Z}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-representable-universally-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9d5aeb9363e6c0460c4d8ca174db9b6e52fab48bca0eb728566dbe3f6bc86cf4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:817e51c552d96ec33710267f0d42dfc2838eadc7c332327cdb183fa75cfeabbd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of\nalgebraic stacks which is representable by algebraic spaces.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is universally closed (as in Properties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0001>), and\n<STRUCT_0003> for every morphism of algebraic stacks <MATH_0003>\nthe morphism of topological spaces\n<MATH_0004> is closed.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ceee4464a2d17b82a787fe016e7678934eb7d5ec10e186bb5785d5abef32fd28", "unit_id": "tag:0512:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0511", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to V$", "MATH_0005": "$|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |V|$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[d] \\\\\n|V| \\ar[r] & |\\mathcal{Z}|\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\longrightarrow\n|V| \\times_{|\\mathcal{Z}|} |\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}|\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Rightarrow$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09aa1f8c8ad23cd19dc339d90766602caa1ad31ba2d799a54bf34d02f2619393", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f409999f8fd90ccec69fe23ff7f3aa8a8aba6b7794e74fb255fa7dd89d25a5da", "source_text": "Assume (1), and let <MATH_0001> be as in (2).\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0002> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0003>.\nBy assumption the morphism <MATH_0004>\nof algebraic spaces is universally closed, in particular the map\n<MATH_0005> is closed. By\nProperties of Stacks, Section <REF_0001>\nin the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nthe horizontal arrows are open and surjective, and moreover\n<MATH_0007>\nis surjective. Hence as the left vertical arrow is closed it follows that\nthe right vertical arrow is closed. This proves (2).\nThe implication (2) <MATH_0008> (1) follows from the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:22cf1d8db38a4b377489515b357a1eba4762d77439348932692c188c7fc2e9c8", "unit_id": "tag:0512:proof"}
